 "stimulus_html": "Use the graph below for questions 3 and 4.\n<p>The two lines on the coordinate plane are graphs of functions <span data-math=\"f\">f</span> and <span data-math=\"g\">g</span>. </p>\n<p><img alt=\"Graph of 2 lines.\" src=\"exercises/media/4dd8b03f869b6fcb.svg\"></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 648682,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"3\">\n  <li>Use the graph to explain why the value of <span data-math=\"f\">f</span> increases by 2 each time the input <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> increases by 1.</li>\n</ol>\n<ol type=\"a\">\n<li>The <span data-math=\"y\">y</span>-axis counts by 2’s so <span data-math=\"f\">f</span> must increase 2 each time the input increases 1.</li>\n<li>There are two graphs so <span data-math=\"f\">f</span> increases by 2 each time the input <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> increases by 1.</li>\n<li><span data-math=\"(0, 0)\">(0, 0)</span> and <span data-math=\"(1, 2)\">(1, 2)</span> are two points on the graph of <span data-math=\"f\">f</span>. Between the two points, <span data-math=\"y\">y</span> increases by 2 and <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> increases by 1.</li>\n<li><span data-math=\"f\">f</span> does not increase by 2 each time <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> increases by 1.</li>\n</ol>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 648683,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"4\" type=\"1\">\n  <li>Use the graph to explain why the value of <span data-math=\"g\">g</span> increases by 2 each time the input <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> increases by 1. <strong>Select two </strong>that apply.</li>\n</ol>\n<ol type=\"a\">\n<li><span data-math=\"f\">f</span> and <span data-math=\"g\">g</span> never intersect and stay an equal distance apart. <span data-math=\"f\">f</span> increases by 2 every time <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> increases by 1, so <span data-math=\"g\">g</span> must do so as well.</li>\n<li>You can’t use the graph because the points are not labeled.</li>\n<li>There are two graphs so <span data-math=\"g\">g</span> increases by 2 each time the input <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> increases by 1.</li>\n<li><span data-math=\"(0, 5)\">(0, 5)</span>and <span data-math=\"(1, 7)\">(1, 7)</span> are points on the graph of <span data-math=\"g\">g</span>.  Between the two points, <span data-math=\"y\">y</span> increases by 2 and <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> increases by 1.</li>\n<li><span data-math=\"(0, 0)\">(0, 0)</span> and <span data-math=\"(1, 2)\">(1, 2)</span> are two points on the graph of <span data-math=\"g\">g</span>. Between the two points, <span data-math=\"y\">y</span> increases by 2 and <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> increases by 1.</li>\n</ol>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  }
 ],
